# 2nd attempt at having robust (and easy to maintain) code for non-deterministic behavior in the model.

## problem being fixed
    Problem with having model_status is that it replicates the logic embedded in model_index.
    Loading models is tricky and requires some work. And increases maintenance burden because of this.
    Also fix problem of iteration count not being properly incremented.


## Solution

    runAlgorithm will submit runs (to limit) if have any instantiated cases when it loads in an existing Study.
    Add a study_properties to Model which can be used to store anything. Just need to settle on key.
    This stores calling info replacing model_status dict.
    Still checking for non-deterministic behavior at the algorithm level.

## Details.
name generation is not sensible as iter_count does not increment in a useful way and we regen params/obs every time as
we run....

1) Model changes
   - modify Model to have a new attribute dict:study_properties used to store any  study properties wanted.
2) Changes to runSubmit
   a) Modify set_model_status to set study_properties['model_status'] to status
   b) remove model_status dict from runSubmit.
   b) Modify runSubmit from_dict/to_dict no longer worry about model_status. Though if present will be used to set study_properties['model_status'] and then remove it.
   e) Modify reset of _logical_info so that iteration info correct. Now have reset_used_models which sets all called models to not_called.
   f) Add method called models to runSubmit which returns a lists of models for a given logical name.
     Uses _logical_info.model_keys and model_index to do this. [Which is another reason why LogicalInfo is not very satisfactory.]
3) Changes to LogicalInfo
   a) Add an attribute called model_keys which is a dict -- key  name, values a list of keys to look up model in model_info
   b) remove models attribute.
   c) remove code than handles models attribute though if present on read in use to set model_keys and then remove it.
   d) And also modified logical_cost so it computes costs (and caches them) as needed. Will break if observations get changed...

4) runAlgorithm
   a) Move submission of existing runs earlier in runAlgorithm. Broadly after it has finished loading up existing runs.
   That will make no determ/iteration count logic much cleaner.


